WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Take a break from building your snowman.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.680
Because for the first time in forever we're doing a theory on Frozen!

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.200
Hello Internet, welcome to Film Theory!

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.480
You know the Frozen lore you thought you knew?

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.400
Well prepare to 'let it go' because today's theory will change everything you thought you knew

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.060
about the adorkable Anna and the incomparable Adeledazeem.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.860
Now Disney Animation has picked up a fun little habit in the last few years of dropping

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.560
hidden Easter eggs throughout their movies. Making it seem like some, or maybe even all, of them

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.460
take place in a larger connected universe.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:52.400
And with Frozen being the biggest animated money maker in, well, ever

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.460
they've  connected Frozen with a whole bunch of other movies.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:59.140
There are plenty of other theories floating around about The Little Mermaid and Tarzan;

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.680
but the connection I'm most interested in today is between Frozen and Tangled.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:07.480
And before you run away thinking you've heard this one because of course there's stuff on the

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:10.080
internet that connects Tangled and Frozen, hear me out.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.880
Because this is a brand new finding that I think is gonna change the way that you see these

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:20.360
two movies. Yes, they're movies about long lost magical Princesses, but the evidence across both

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.980
points to a huge secret about the relation between Anna, Elsa, and Rapunzel.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:29.800
Specifically, that Anna and Elsa, aren't the sisters in these movies.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.500
That's right, Anna and Elsa: not sisters!

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:37.240
I mean is that really hard to believe? Look at the family portrait. One of these things is not like the others.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.360
Someone looks a whole lot like the milkman.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:44.480
Nope! it's not Anna and Elsa who are the sisters, but rather Elsa and Rapunzel.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.400
And sure! You may be shaking your head now, but the backing for this theory is real.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:51.320
From the movies lore, to Disney's own information.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.920
And if you stick with me, I think you're gonna agree.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.380
The first pieces of evidence we have come from Disney itself.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:00.580
Who've slipped bits and pieces of information about Frozen's lore since the movie came out.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:02.880
First, Frozen writer and director Jennifer Lee

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.180
confirmed a huge point in a Reddit AMA about King and Queen...

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:07.180
uhh...

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.960
King and Queen...What are their names?

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.760
Agnarr and Iduna?

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.460
Really? Scandanavia we need to talk about your naming conventions here.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:18.660
In any case, while Agnarr and Iduna are lost at sea,

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.320
they're not going off on any old 3 hour tour, they're sailing for a wedding.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.780
It was also confirmed that this isn't just any wedding they're going to:

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.320
it's Rapunzel's wedding from the end of Tangled.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.920
That's huge right there!

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.240
We already have a solid connection between the movies in two ways:

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.880
Space and time.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.340
Looking at a map this makes total sense based on where these movies take place.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:43.980
It's been pretty well established that Frozen's location of Arendelle is a hybrid of Arednal and Bergen Norway

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:49.760
It's so well known in fact that the Norway zone of Epcot was completely overrun after the movie came out

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:55.680
and Disney had special Frozen tours set up in Norway to handle all the crazy Elsa fans storming into the country.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:00.620
Probably the only time in Disney's history that people actually were excited to go visit Epcot.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:06.900
Tangled is likely to take place around the corner just across the North Sea in modern Germany in a fictional city called Corona.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:11.540
This matches where the Rapunzel story was originally based since it was one of Grimm's fairy tales.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:15.260
So they're definitely close enough to bump into each other out on their royal yachts

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:18.580
Or royal ice barges, I guess?

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.120
I don't know what you guys do that far north.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.200
We also know when they connect in time.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.540
Based on the hints Disney has already dropped,

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.980
we know these movies are three years apart.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.860
Closer than any other Disney Princess timeline.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:31.580
We start with extra scenes at the end of Tangled.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.440
Where Rapunzel and Flinn get married

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.140
and start their happily ever after.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.700
We know at this point that Agnarr and Iduna are supposed to be on their way to a wedding,

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.080
Rapunzel's wedding,

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.340
but they never make it.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.080
When the main story of Frozen starts,

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.840
we're specifically told that it happens

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.000
three years after the shipwreck.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:50.460
Which means exactly three years after Tangled's wedding.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:53.240
What's fascinating is that this timing plays out,

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.520
both in the movie and in real life at the same time.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:58.660
In the movies releases themselves.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.600
Tangled's release was November 24th, 2010

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:03.660
Frozen was released almost exactly

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:09.240
3 years later to the day on November 27th, 2013

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.120
and picks up exactly three years later

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:12.900
as soon as you start the movie.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.640
The timelines follow each other both in the real world

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:18.120
and in their own universe which is brilliant

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.520
and also, not by accident.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.440
We know based on the Wikis that Rapunzel is

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:23.600
18 after her movie

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.520
She gets married shortly after she shows up

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.460
back at the castle

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:29.220
despite the fact that Flinn says it took many years.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:31.380
"After years and years of asking"

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:32.960
If you need proof for that,

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.600
Rapunzel already says the he's lying in that line:

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:36.800
"Eugene"

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.200
If the wedding were to take any longer than that

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.200
Rapunzel's hair would have grown out

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.180
And sadly a delayed wedding would also mean that

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.200
Pascal would not be in the wedding party...

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.300
He'd be dead,

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.520
based on the average lifespan for veiled chameleon's.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.500
Sorry man it's called the circle of life.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:51.100
*Blow's raspberry*

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.000
So Rapunzel is 18 at the wedding

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.100
And when Frozen happens 3 years later.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.100
We know Elsa to be 21

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.400
In short some simple math tells us Elsa and Rapunzel

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.300
are the same age.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.800
And I mean exactly the same age

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.000
They were born at the same time

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.660
They're twins.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.860
Fraternal not identical obviously.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.100
But now I know you're saying that that's just ridiculous.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.860
Yes, the movies are connected

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.660
and yes, they overlap and stuff

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:18.740
but it's impossible that the two are twins, right?

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:19.480
Wrong!

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:21.640
In fact it's completely possible!

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:24.180
to prove it i'll start out with some good, old fashioned biology.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.700
Loyal theorists know that some of my favourite theories

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.860
here, and on Game Theory, are backed by genetics

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:30.860
and this one is no exception.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.580
One of the reasons people usually assume

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.280
that Elsa HAS to be the daughter of

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:37.220
Agnarr and Iduna is that her eyes are blue

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.140
just like her mothers.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:39.760
Now the genetics around eye colour

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.780
are slightly more complicated than we were taught

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.380
in eighth grade science class

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.580
but to roughly simplify, to prove the point,

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.760
both blue eyes and green eyes are recessive

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.700
so you must have two light eye alleles

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.000
to get a blue eyed kid.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.480
When one parent has green eyes and the other has blue

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:54.600
like you see in Frozen.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:56.940
The odds of Anna or Elsa individually having

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.900
blue eyes is 50%.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.580
Yay for the recessive Scandinavian gene pool.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.020
but it's just as genetically likely for Elsa

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:06.280
to belong to the King and Queen in Tangled.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.680
Who, for the life of me, i couldn't find their names

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:11.360
turns out Agnarr and Iduna aren't the only ones

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:12.780
with blue and green eyes

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:15.000
King and Queen Tangled are yet another

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.940
blue and green eyed royal couple.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:18.380
Weird coincidence, right?

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:19.360
Maybe..

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:20.480
Maybe not..

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.160
At the very least this means that

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.860
genetically they have the same

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.300
probability as the Frozen royal couple

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.780
of ending up with a blue eyed baby like Elsa.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:29.940
But that's not all!

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:31.940
Beyond eyes, we can also tell they're twins

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:34.160
based on the fact that they're both left-handed.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.520
22% of twins are left-handed

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:38.820
which is more than double the world average.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:41.140
For Elsa, we see her doing the important things

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.420
in the movies as a lefty.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.820
Her primary ice-shooting hand is left.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:46.780
She creates Olaf with her left hand.

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:48.000
Touches her face left.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.380
Unties her braid left.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.480
and even tries to save Anna

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:52.300
with a crucial, left-handed ice attack.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.980
It's a pretty similar story over on the Tangled side.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.940
Rapunzel is definitely more ambidextrous

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.680
than Elsa is and she does things with both hands.

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:01.480
However she shows a preference

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.380
for her left hand in crucial activities.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:06.000
Especially ones where she has to act on instinct.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.580
She paints and brushes her hair

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:09.380
both with left and right hands

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:12.200
but in an emergency, she brandishes her frying pan

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.860
with her left hand, or bats lefty with it.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:16.540
She naturally reaches out for her

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.420
parents lantern with her left hand.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:19.820
Holds candles with her left.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:22.160
Holds Pascal left and throws left.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:23.820
And just so you don't think i'm playing favourites

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:26.040
other characters are distinctly right-handed.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.400
In Frozen, Anna always knocks right-handed

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.280
and reaches out with her right hand.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.060
In Tangled, Eugene swings his sword right

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:36.160
points right, and touches Rapunzels face right-handed.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:37.280
But all this left-handedness

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.260
has to come from somewhere, right?

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:39.820
or left?

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:41.300
one of the two *ba-dum tiss*

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:42.980
Luckily it happens that Mummy Tangled

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.300
happens to be likely left-handed.

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:46.380
We don't get a lot of camera time

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:47.880
with the Kings and Queens in general

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.200
but Rapunzel's mother is shown

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:50.680
with a left-handed preference

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.140
in most scenes she's in.

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:53.740
Holding Rapunzel left-handed.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:54.940
Gesturing left-handed

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.300
and reaching out to touch Rapunzel

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:57.900
left-handed after seeing her for

00:07:57.940 --> 00:07:59.700
the first time in 18 years.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:01.580
There isn't enough evidence on the Frozen side

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.040
to say whether Agnarr and Iduna

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.000
are left-handed or not.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.680
But we know the genetics line up for Tangled.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.200
And finally we have hair.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.960
Honestly, none of these parents are

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.640
likely to produce children with bright blonde hair

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.340
like either Rapunzel or Elsa.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.080
But, as we learn in Tangled,

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:17.880
Rapunzel's blonde hair comes from

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:19.520
the magic her mother absorbed

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.140
from a bright yellow flower.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.460
If in fact these two are twins

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:26.100
it would also explain Elsa's unusually

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:27.540
vibrant blonde hair.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.080
Which is surprisingly, more plausible

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:30.320
than the slim genetic chance

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:32.320
Iduna and Agnarr have of producing

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.100
a toe-headed ice Princess.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:36.320
So at this point, the location of the movie,

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:37.480
timing of the movie,

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:38.860
and biology of the movie

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:40.740
all support Rapunzel and Elsa

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.620
being Disney's true first

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.460
magical Princess sisters.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.820
But what about the really exciting stuff?

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.960
What about their actual magic?

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.280
If these two are indeed twins

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:51.280
like I'm saying they are

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:53.240
they should have the same powers, right?

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:54.520
I don't know if you've seen these movies lately

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:55.500
but ice blasting?

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:58.400
Definitely not the same as ole healing hair over here.

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.840
Well hang onto your anthropomorphic reindeer!

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:03.360
Because there's even more evidence to this theory.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:05.000
First of all, it's really important

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.300
to reiterate the fact that Elsa and Rapunzel

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:09.020
are the only two Princesses

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:10.860
to EVER have magical powers

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.000
in a Disney movie.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:14.680
Seriously, the only two Princesses

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:17.580
in the 80 year history of Disney films

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:18.500
who can use magic!

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:21.200
That's pretty incredible if you think about it.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.220
And it's not an accident.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:23.980
This doesn't happen just because

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:25.540
they're cool Northern Europeans

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.100
who share the same magical universe.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:30.100
It's because they share the same magical mum.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.460
Like I said before, Rapunzel absorbs magic

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.080
from a healing potion her mum drinks

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.120
before she's born.

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:37.120
This is how we explain Rapunzel's magic

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:38.040
for the rest of the movie

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:40.980
and for better or worst it kinda makes sense.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.660
The writers clearly took the time to build in

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.760
a backstory that justifies her magic

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:46.800
instead of it having to come out of nowhere.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.580
So, where's the backstory in Frozen?

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:51.520
Where's our magical history lesson?

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:52.720
Is it laziness?

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:53.700
Well, no.

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:55.080
This is an animation team who

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.340
bothered to draw in Snow White

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:59.000
and Sleeping Beauty in to Rapunzel's book collection.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:09:59.860
If they left something out

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:02.380
it's because there's another explanation.

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.460
No one in the Frozen royal family has magic

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:06.140
or was ever exposed to it.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:08.580
These are the muggley-ist Disney characters out there.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.680
Even when the royal family takes Elsa

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:11.600
to the rock trolls

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:13.280
Agnarr can't answer right away

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:15.880
whether Elsa was born with magic or cursed with it.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.540
"Born with the powers, or cursed?"

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:18.400
"-uh.. Born."

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:20.140
What an oddly specific detail you've

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:21.000
included there Disney.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.580
But THIS is the reason.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.680
When Agnarr stutters in front of the rock trolls,

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.440
he's showing a natural reaction.

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:27.920
'Was she born with these powers?'

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.820
'Uh... y- yes?'

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:31.500
He doesn't know because he wasn't

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:33.560
there when Elsa was born with magic.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.300
Ever wonder why Agnarr and Iduna

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:36.340
never show any surprise about

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:37.520
Elsa's magical powers?

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:39.840
Like, wouldn't you just find it a little bit starting?

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:42.100
Worth a trip to the paediatrician at least.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.040
We never see them doing normal things

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.040
you'd expect parents to do in this situation.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.520
They don't try to cure Elsa

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:48.880
they don't even seem to look for answers

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:50.420
about where her powers came from.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.420
Don't you think thats a little bit strange?

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.240
Well it's not if you consider

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:56.880
that they already know where her powers come from.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:58.160
Her real mother.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.840
The same that gave Rapunzel her powers.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.560
But okay, enough beating around the bush

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.360
let's actually talk about that magic.

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:06.100
One of Frozen's biggest criticisms,

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.100
leveled at it from

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.540
Honest Trailers to Cinema Sins

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:10.640
is that Elsa's power set has always

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:11.680
seemed a bit weird.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:14.680
"Meet Elsa, a manic depressive princess"

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:16.620
"with a confusing set of powers"

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.740
"like - creating life?"

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:21.560
"you're alive? / Uhm.. I think so?"

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:23.280
"they kind of gloss over that one"

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.560
Yeah she freezes stuff

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:26.900
causes major destruction and blizzards

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:28.820
builds ice castles, all that.

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:31.360
But then she also brings things to life

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:34.720
creating sentient creatures like Olaf and Marshmellow.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:36.760
Literally, it's all over the place!

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:39.200
At first it actually seems like Elsa and Rapunzel

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:40.880
have opposite powers.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.100
With Elsa stopping everything from growing

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:45.660
and Rapunzel making everything young and new again.

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:47.580
A Yin and Yang sort of situation.

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:48.760
But if you look closer

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:50.940
their powers are actually more similar than you think.

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:51.840
Let's go through it:

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:53.180
In the ending to both movies

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:54.940
the Princesses save someone they love.

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:56.220
In Frozen, it's Anna

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:58.780
In Tangled its Flynn, or Eugene

00:11:58.780 --> 00:11:59.860
or whatever his name is.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.840
To start both scenes the true love character

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:02.720
saves the Princess.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:04.540
Eugene saves Rapunzel from Mother Gothel

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:06.600
and Anna saves Elsa from Prince Hans.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:09.180
In doing so they both die in the process:

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:10.120
Anna by freezing

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.700
and Eugene with a stab wound.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:13.320
Anna exhales her last breath

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:14.620
Eugene falls limp.

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:16.560
These guys are gone.

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:18.600
At this point each of our Power Princesses

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:19.960
literally hugs the true love

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:22.140
for an awkwardly long minute of sobbing

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:24.520
and then suddenly discover a new power

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:25.880
they never thought they had.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.620
The exact same power.

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.480
Reviving the dead.

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:30.820
Giving things life.

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:32.640
In Tangled it's giving Mother Gothel

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:33.440
and Eugene life.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.360
In Frozen it's giving snowmen

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:36.100
and Anna life.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:37.120
Coincidence?

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:38.500
Not a chance!

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:40.240
It's the exact same power

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:42.880
executed the exact same way!

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:44.580
Their powers aren't opposite!

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:46.180
In fact, they're twins!

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.920
Just like the Princesses themselves

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:50.620
Elsa did inherit the power to revive things

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:51.900
just like Rapunzel.

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:53.460
She just, also ends up with some

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:54.560
nice ice upgrades.

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:56.840
In short, everything in these movies

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.460
from the setting, the background

00:12:58.460 --> 00:12:59.980
the lore, 
the genetics

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.200
the magical powers

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:03.700
even the structure of their own stories

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:05.360
are direct parallels.

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:06.520
So now I ask you,

00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:07.360
look at the evidence

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:09.520
and look at the story one more time

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:11.420
through a new lens.

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:13.700
Once upon a time in Corona,

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:15.020
a Kingdom in Northern Germany

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:16.580
a sick Queen drinks a magical

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:18.140
healing potion, made from a

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:19.420
magical yellow flower

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:20.680
right before giving birth.

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:22.020
She has twin daughters.

00:13:22.020 --> 00:13:23.540
The girls are blonde, as both

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:25.620
are infused with the magic of the flower.

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:27.340
One daughter immediately demonstrates

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:29.140
magical healing powers as you sing

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:29.900
and the other one...

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:31.680
doesn't really seem to do all that much.

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:33.840
Mother Gothel discovers that Baby 1

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:35.080
will keep her young forever,

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:36.640
but she can't just snip some hair

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:38.540
so she has to take the whole baby.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.060
Which she does by kidnapping her

00:13:40.060 --> 00:13:41.560
and locking her up in a tower.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.560
King and Queen Tangled are heartbroken

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:44.860
that Baby 1 is stolen

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:46.360
and they realise that they can't risk

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.100
losing Baby 2 if she's ever

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:49.540
discovered to have magical powers.

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.420
They know Corona isn't safe

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:52.740
and send Baby 2 on a trip

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:54.500
across the North Sea to the neighbouring

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:55.720
kingdom of Arendelle

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:57.540
to live with Agnarr and Iduna

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.400
far away from Mother Gothel.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.080
In Arendelle, the King and Queen

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:03.360
eventually realise that Elsa does indeed

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:04.760
have magical powers too.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:06.600
Unprepared to raise a magical child,

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:08.060
they try to hide Elsa's powers

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:10.100
to protect her from being kidnapped

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:11.520
like her sister, Rapunzel.

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:12.780
Closing up the castle

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:13.640
Limiting the staff

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:15.040
Hiding Elsa indoors

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.180
It's to keep the word from getting out to Corona

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:19.740
that there was another Princess born with magic.

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:21.340
And to protect their own daughter Anna

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.240
from accidentally spilling Elsa's secret

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:25.180
or becoming the target of a kidnapping herself

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:26.640
they have her memory wiped.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.480
The bad rep Agnarr and Iduna get

00:14:28.480 --> 00:14:30.040
is all in the name of helping to keep

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:32.880
Elsa safe until her sister Rapunzel reappears.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:34.680
And eventually the two find each other

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:37.620
when Rapunzel ends up in Arendelle

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.280
at the end of Frozen.

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:41.120
So is that the TRUE origin story

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:42.880
of Anna, Elsa and Rapunzel?

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:44.380
I guess we'll have to see what happens

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:46.000
in Frozen 2.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.900
But Hey..    That's just a theory..

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:51.560
A FILM THEORY

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:53.720
aaannd.. CUT!

